  {
   "topic": "Power derating",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Full rated power is allowed up to 70 °C ambient. Above that it falls in a straight line to zero at 155 °C, or at 125 °C for the 01005 and 0201 sizes."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "0201 and 0402 parts carry no marking. ±5% parts show three digits, ±0.5% to ±2% parts four, the last digit being the power of ten. 0603 ±1% parts are too small for four digits: an E96 value is shown as its two-digit index and a multiplier letter, and an E24 value outside E96 takes the ±5% code with a line under the middle digit. Jumpers of every size show a single 0."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Hand soldering",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "Iron at 350±10℃ for under 3 s, with the tip kept off the resistor body."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Environments that degrade performance",
   "page": 13,
   "text": "Performance can suffer at high temperature; near sea air or in corrosive gases such as Cl2, H2S, NH3, SO2 and NO2; in contact with unverified liquids such as water, oil, chemicals or organic solvents; under unverified resin or paint coatings; and where boards are cleaned with water or water-soluble cleaners after soldering, no-clean flux included."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Storage and handling",
   "page": 13,
   "text": "Keep at 25±5℃ and 30%～70%RH, use within two years on a first-in first-out basis, keep boxes the right way up and never drop them, since a fall can damage the terminations or body."
  }
